he large backdrop wall and the smaller bouquets on the stage and in the orchestra (Frames 12–15) — are **bright yellow**. This is a consistent, prominent decorative element.\n\n---\n\n**5) Color of large logos/emblems:**\n\n- The large “N” logo on the stage floor is **white**.\n- The Nobel Prize emblem on the podium (visible in close-ups) is **gold and blue**.\n- The Swedish royal coat of arms (above the organ) includes **blue, yellow, and red**, but it is not part of the stage decoration per se — it’s part of the hall’s permanent fixtures.\n\nThe most prominent logo *on the stage* is the white “N” on blue, so **white and blue** are the primary logo colors.\n\n---\n\n**6) Consistency of color patterns across the stage:**\n\nYes, the color scheme is highly consistent:\n\n- The **blue carpet** covers the entire stage floor in every wide shot.\n- The **yellow floral backdrop** is consistently visible behind the podium.\n- The **yellow floral accents** are repeated along the front edge of the stage and in the orchestra pit.\n- The **gold/yellow** accents on the balcony railings and decorative panels match the floral color.\n- The **white “N” logo** is centered and unchanging.\n\nThere is no variation or inconsistency in the core color palette across frames.\n\n---\n\n**Verification of Answer ‘2’ (“Blue and red”):**\n\nThe claim that the primary color scheme is **“Blue and red”** is **incorrect**.\n\n- While **blue** is indeed a dominant color (stage carpet, logo background), **red is not a primary color** in the stage decoration.\n- Red appears only minimally:\n  - A single red rose on the speaker’s lapel (Frames 2–4, 10–11) — a personal accessory, not part of the stage design.\n  - The Swedish coat of arms includes red, but it is a background element of the hall, not the ceremony’s stage decoration.\n  - No red carpets, flowers, backdrops, or logos are used in the stage design.\n\nThe actual dominant colors are **blue and yellow**, with white and gold as accents.\n\n---\n\n✅ **Final Answer: The correct primary color scheme of the stage decoration is BLUE and YELLOW. The answer ‘2’ (Blue and red) is INCORRECT.**'}, {'batch_start': 30, 'batch_end': 60, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_1384.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_1385.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_1386.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_1454.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_1455.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_1456.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_1457.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_1458.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_1459.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_1460.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_1461.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_1462.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_1463.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_1464.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_2893.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_2894.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_2895.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_2896.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_2897.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_2898.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_2899.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_2900.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_2901.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSK