tterns across the stage:**\n\nThe color pattern is **highly consistent** across all frames: blue carpet, yellow/gold backdrop and flowers, white “N” logo, and red accents in the surrounding hall (balcony railings, audience seating). The repetition of blue and yellow/gold creates a unified, formal, and ceremonial palette.\n\n---\n\n**Verification of Answer ‘2’ (“Blue and red”):**\n\nWhile **blue** is undeniably the dominant color of the stage carpet and a key part of the scheme, **red is not a primary color of the stage decoration itself**. Red appears only in the **audience seating and balcony railings** — elements of the hall’s permanent architecture, not the temporary stage design. The floral arrangements, backdrop, and logo are yellow/gold and white, not red.\n\nTherefore, **“Blue and red” is not the correct primary color scheme for the stage decoration**. The accurate dominant stage color scheme is **blue and yellow/gold**.\n\n---\n\n✅ **Final Verdict: Answer ‘2’ (“Blue and red”) is INCORRECT.**  \nThe primary colors of the stage decoration are **blue and yellow/gold**.'}], 'formatted_responses': ['\n=== Batch 0-30 (30 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_0329.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_0330.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_0331.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_0332.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_0333.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_0334.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_0335.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_0336.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_0337.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_0338.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/YlQugR7KSKg/frames/frame_0339.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/vi